SET ECHO OFF
* ============================================================
* MCC_EXHAUSTIVE_FULL_X64_REGRESSION_CANARIES_SETMODERN_VB_10_1.DTS
*
* TARGET: x64
*
* Purpose:
*   Public-surface regression harness for DotTalk++ current build.
*
* Scope:
*   - Public SET syntax
*   - Core table navigation / display
*   - CDX/LMDB ordered access through public commands
*   - SEEK / FIND / LOCATE canaries
*   - SMARTLIST / WHERE / SET FILTER observations
*   - tuple / table-buffer / calcwrite smoke
*   - SQLite / DotScript / TUPTALK smoke
*
* Explicitly separated:
*   1) AUTOMATED SAFE CORE
*   2) KNOWN-FAIL / OBSERVATION CANARIES
*   3) MANUAL / INTERACTIVE / DESTRUCTIVE
*
* Public index workflow:
*   SET INDEX TO <table>.cdx
*   SET ORDER TO TAG <tag>
*   ASCEND / DESCEND
*   SET ORDER TO 0
*
* Public rebuild workflow:
*   BUILDLMDB
*
* Important:
*   BUILDLMDB is interactive/destructive and is NOT run in the automated core.
*   REINDEX remains transitional/legacy coverage only.
*
* Dataset note:
*   This script may be run against a live working dataset, not a pristine fixture.
*   Do not assume factory field values unless restored outside this DTS.
* ============================================================

* ------------------------------------------------------------
* HISTORY / REDACTION NOTES
* 2026-05-13:
*   - Restored hard x64 workspace fences after isolated table tests.
*   - Moved active x64 memo reopen/update bug into separate canary:
*       MEMO_X64_REOPEN_CANARY_20260513.dts
*   - Removed MEMO64 from the automated integrated harness so it cannot
*     poison later table/index/relation sections by leaving MEMO_X64 current.
*   - Redacted solved DATE comparison known-fail canaries:
*       DATE()+2 > DATE(), DATE()-2 < DATE(), CTOD()+1, CTOD()-1.
*     These remain covered by the baseline DATE ALGEBRA section above.
*   - Redacted solved ORDER-ENTRY and INDEXSEEK observation canaries.
*     These are now covered by the core public index workflow and TEACHERS/STUDENTS
*     SEEK/FIND/INDEXSEEK probes.
*   - Removed DEV LMDB utility probes from automated core. Public CDX/LMDB access
*     remains covered by SET INDEX TO <table>.cdx + SET ORDER TO TAG <tag>.
* ------------------------------------------------------------

SETPATH DBF DBF/X64
SETPATH INDEXES INDEXES/X64

ECHO ===== V4 REGRESSION START =====
COLOR DEFAULT
VERSION

